Addressed the "not fully atomic" finding on the \`lastPullSyncAt\` stamping fix (commit 528c7c5e9): \`ExternalCrmSyncService.updateSyncTimestamp\` no longer reload-then-writes the whole provider config — it now calls a new \`crmDb.updateLeadListCrmSyncStatus\`, a targeted DynamoDB nested-attribute \`UpdateExpression\` that only touches \`externalCrmSyncConfigs.<provider>.{lastPushSyncAt|lastPullSyncAt|lastSyncStatus|lastSyncError|lastSyncErrorCategory|lastSyncErrorCount|updatedAt}\`, never reading or rewriting sibling fields like \`contactFieldMapping\`. A concurrent config save can no longer be clobbered by a status update racing it, regardless of timing.

